{0 Resources}

A curated list of talks, papers, and related projects for understanding
property-based testing and the ideas behind Hedgehog.

{1 Hedgehog family}

- {{:https://hedgehog.qa}Haskell Hedgehog} — The original implementation
  by Jacob Stanley. Hedgehog for OCaml follows the same design.
- {{:https://github.com/hedgehogqa/scala-hedgehog}Scala Hedgehog} — Scala
  port with similar architecture.
- {{:https://github.com/hedgehogqa/fsharp-hedgehog}F# Hedgehog} — F#
  port.
- {{:https://github.com/hedgehogqa/kotlin-hedgehog}Kotlin Hedgehog} —
  Kotlin port.

{1 Talks}

- {{:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AIv_9T0ab-8}Gens N' Roses: Appetite for Reduction}
  by Jacob Stanley — Explains why integrated shrinking matters and how
  rose trees make it work. This is {i the} talk for understanding
  Hedgehog's design.
- {{:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MIYhFkzGEL0}Choosing properties for property-based testing}
  by Scott Wlaschin — Practical advice on what properties to test.
- {{:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zi0rHwfiX1Q}Building on Developers' Intuitions}
  by John Hughes — From the creator of QuickCheck, on making PBT
  accessible.

{1 Papers}

- {{:https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/351240.351266}QuickCheck: A Lightweight Tool for Random Testing of Haskell Programs}
  by Koen Claessen and John Hughes (2000) — The original QuickCheck paper.
- {{:https://proper-testing.github.io/papers/finding-race-conditions.pdf}Finding Race Conditions in Erlang with QuickCheck and PULSE}
  by Koen Claessen et al. — State machine testing for concurrency.
- {{:https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/2661136.2661159}Producing Wrong Data Without Doing Anything Obviously Wrong!}
  by Alex Groce et al. — On the importance of good shrinking.

{1 Books}

- {{:https://propertesting.com}Property-Based Testing with PropEr, Erlang, and Elixir}
  by Fred Hebert — Excellent practical introduction to PBT concepts,
  applicable across languages.
- {{:https://www.manning.com/books/the-joy-of-kotlin}The Joy of Kotlin}
  by Pierre-Yves Saumont — Includes a chapter on property-based testing.

{1 OCaml ecosystem}

- {{:https://github.com/c-cube/qcheck}QCheck} — The established OCaml
  PBT library.
- {{:https://github.com/janestreet/ppx_quickcheck}ppx_quickcheck} — Jane
  Street's PBT with ppx derivation.
- {{:https://github.com/ocaml-multicore/dscheck}DSCheck} — Model checking
  for concurrent OCaml programs.
